2026-11-03 18:55 binary-worker start. Plan: OpenSSL 3.5.9 (LTS, supported to 2030-04-08; 3.6 support ended 2026-11-01, 3.0 ended 2026-09) built no-shared/no-module/no-autoload-config with -fPIC, linked statically into Net::SSLeay 1.96. OPENSSLDIR=/etc/ssl so IO::Socket::SSL's own lookup finds the system store on Debian/Ubuntu (/etc/ssl/certs hashed), RHEL 9+/Fedora (/etc/ssl/cert.pem) and macOS (/etc/ssl/cert.pem); packed Mozilla::CA is IO::Socket::SSL's fallback where none is found (RHEL 8 family, images without ca-certificates); SSL_CERT_FILE/SSL_CERT_DIR override. no-autoload-config keeps the static OpenSSL from reading the host's openssl.cnf (written for another OpenSSL). Found (lib/, for mcp-hub-worker): _base_url keeps the listen URL's query, so hub.listen 'https://…?cert=…&key=…' makes 'mcp-hub config' print '…?cert=…&key=…/hub' and status/refresh/reload call a broken base (verified with perl -Ilib).

